-- title:
--   Mamikon's theorem: the swept area is half the integral of squared segment lengths
-- statement:
--   The generalized Mamikon theorem of the source: if a family of tangent segments is generated by a continuously differentiable base curve z whose derivative at each interior parameter is parallel to the wall direction v_t, with continuously varying lengths α(t), and the family has no self-overlap on the open parameter rectangle, then the area of the region swept over a turning interval of length less than π is exactly half the integral of the squared lengths. The statement is the mission's abridgement of the source's Theorem 7.4.1, stated for exactly the smooth, non-self-overlapping families that the endgame applies it to, with the turning interval bounded by a < b < a + π.
-- source:
--   Baek (2024), Optimality of Gerver's Sofa, arXiv:2411.19826, Theorem 7.4.1 (the generalized Mamikon theorem; Step 3 machinery)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Gerver_arena
import Definitions.Def_Gerver_monotone
import Definitions.Def_Gerver_sofa

namespace Gerver

/-- Step 3 machinery (Theorem 7.4.1, generalized Mamikon theorem): the area of
the region swept out by a continuously differentiable family of tangent
segments — base curve z with z'(t) parallel to v_t at each t, segment lengths
α(t), no self-overlap on the open parameter rectangle — is exactly half the
integral of the squared lengths over the interval of turning. -/
theorem mamikon_area (z : ℝ → ℝ × ℝ) (α : ℝ → ℝ) {a b : ℝ}
    (hab : a < b) (hb : b < a + Real.pi)
    (hz : ContDiffOn ℝ 1 z (Set.Icc a b)) (hα : ContinuousOn α (Set.Icc a b))
    (htan : ∀ t ∈ Set.Ioo a b, dot (derivWithin z (Set.Icc a b) t) (u t) = 0)
    (hinj : ∀ t ∈ Set.Ioo a b, ∀ s ∈ Set.Ioo 0 1, ∀ t' ∈ Set.Ioo a b,
      ∀ s' ∈ Set.Ioo 0 1,
      z t + scale (s * α t) (v t) = z t' + scale (s' * α t') (v t') →
        t = t' ∧ s = s') :
    area (swept z α a b) = ∫ t in a..b, α t ^ 2 / 2 := by
  sorry

end Gerver
